timeshift-ssh (25.12.4+ssh19) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Restore: require an EFI System Partition when the snapshot came from a UEFI system - it was defaulting to 'keep on root', so the ESP was never mounted, the snapshot's EFI payload landed on ext4 and grub-install failed with 'cannot find EFI directory'
  * Restore: never use an ESP on a different disk from the root device - both front ends defaulted to the ESP of the machine running the restore, which would overwrite the live system's boot loader
  * Restore: show the snapshot's original layout against the target selection, and block on a missing / or /boot/efi
  * Restore: capture each post-restore step's output to /var/log/timeshift/restore-steps.log on the restored system

